---
import Desktop from '../layouts/Desktop.astro';
import WindowTitle from '../components/WindowTitle.astro';
const palette = ['#09170e', '#ffffff', '#704da0', '#cbb8e8', '#52705a', '#baff70', '#a8c2aa', '#ffe16d', '#ff8b78', '#a95070', '#559ab0', '#bce4f0'];
const tools = ['M4 4h16v16H4z', 'm4 17 12-12 3 3L7 20H4zm10-10 3 3', 'm5 15 8-10 7 6-8 10H9zM9 21h12', 'M14 4 4 14l6 6L20 10zM4 14h12M20 15s-4 4-1 6 4-2 1-6', 'M5 5h14M12 5v15M8 20h8', 'M5 19 19 5', 'M4 7h16v11H4z', 'M12 4a8 8 0 1 0 0 16 8 8 0 0 0 0-16', 'M4 19c3-16 7 8 16-14', 'M12 3 15 9 21 10 16.5 14.5 17.5 21 12 18 6.5 21 7.5 14.5 3 10 9 9Z'];
const notes = [
  {title: 'My current role', paragraphs: [
    "I work under my local School District as a Substitute Teacher, mostly working for former teachers of my own that need a sub every now and then. I was formerly a tutor under the same district, so after graduating from university, I applied to become a Substitute Teacher as a way to both make an income and be able to continue my career in software development on the side.",
    "For me, a typical day is set up by the teacher I am a substitute for, mostly watching over students as they do individual work. Some days I run tests and other exams for the teachers, and have even done some labs for science classes when necessary. I keep the students on track for their teachers while they're away, so that when they come back it hopefully feels like no time was lost for the class.",
  ]},
  {title: 'Age groups', paragraphs: [
    "I typically work with ages 14 - 18, as I tend to substitute for High School teachers. While it is a small range of ages, you would be surprised how working with a Freshman in high school is vastly different from working with a Senior. With the younger grades I have to be more stern on behavior and help find ways for them to communicate what they need better, while with the older groups I have to give more reassurance that they're on the right track and confidence that they can achieve what they need to do. I try to be a comfortable space for all the students I watch over to be in, and offer tutoring and guidance when asked in any of their classes.",
    "Having a substitute teacher is always a way for students to practice responsibility and respect when it comes to having a stranger suddenly be your teacher for the day. I always tell my students, because they are high schoolers, that they are old enough and have had enough experience in school to understand their responsibilities when it comes to their work and behavior. So while I may correct them on behavior now and then, I never stare over shoulders for the students to get their work done. The time they have with me should teach them that work should still be done even when no one is pushing them to do so.",
  ]},
  {title: 'Responsibilities', paragraphs: [
    "My day-to-day responsibilities are simple: Take attendance for each class, assign the work for the day and explain expectations set by the teacher, and make sure classroom rules are followed while in the class. I am trusted to manage the classroom to the extent that my class is not disruptive, is following school and classroom rules, and that in the event of an emergency I can safely guide and take care of my class.",
  ]},
  {title: 'From teaching to development', prompt: 'Share specific examples of skills I’ve demonstrated while teaching and how I can apply them to software development.'},
];
---
<Desktop page="Current work" description="Katelyn Langley’s current work as a substitute teacher and its connection to software development.">
<section class="window paint-window">
<WindowTitle title="current-work.bmp — Paint" />
<div class="paint-menu" aria-hidden="true"><span><u>F</u>ile</span><span><u>E</u>dit</span><span><u>V</u>iew</span><span><u>I</u>mage</span><span><u>C</u>olors</span><span><u>H</u>elp</span></div>
<div class="paint-workspace">
<aside class="paint-tools" aria-hidden="true">{tools.map((path, i) => <span class:list={["paint-tool", { "paint-tool-selected": i === 1 }]}><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d={path} /></svg></span>)}<div class="paint-brushes"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></aside>
<div class="paint-canvas-surround"><div class="paint-canvas">
<header class="paint-intro"><h1>Substitute Teaching</h1><svg class="paint-underline" viewBox="0 0 460 18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10Q90 2 190 9T455 7M10 15Q180 6 390 13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg><p>I currently work as a substitute teacher.</p></header>
<div class="paint-notes">{notes.map((note, i) => <section class:list={["paint-note", `paint-note-${i}`]}><div>{note.prompt && <p class="paint-placeholder-label">TO BE ADDED</p>}<h2>{note.title}</h2>{note.paragraphs ? note.paragraphs.map(paragraph => <p>{paragraph}</p>) : <p>{note.prompt}</p>}</div></section>)}</div>
</div></div>
</div>
<div class="paint-palette" aria-hidden="true"><span class="paint-current-color"><i></i><i></i></span><div>{palette.map(color => <span style={`background:${color}`}></span>)}</div><span class="paint-color-caption">A little color goes a long way.</span></div>
<div class="paint-status"><span>Current work · Substitute teacher</span><span>Room to learn. Room to create.</span></div>
</section>
</Desktop>
